"Re-Intervention [iOS / Android / Desktop] (https://tutorials.one-sec.app/en/articles/3035202)\nciteturn4view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn3view3\",\"id\":4}); Total lines: 83\nL0: cite0†Help & Tutorials L1: \nL2: cite1†Contact us†riedel.wtf L3: \nL4: How can we help?\nL5: \nL6: In this article\nL7: \nL8: cite2†What are Re-Interventions? cite3†iOS Tutorial cite4†Step 1 cite5†Step 2 cite6†Step 3 cite7†Step 4 cite8†Troubleshooting cite9†What if I selected the wrong app? cite10†What if the app picker crashes or does not show any apps? cite11†Android Tutorial cite12†Desktop Tutorial L9: \nL10: # Re-Intervention [iOS / Android / Desktop]\nL11: \nL12: Edited Monday, January 20 2025\nL13: # What are Re-Interventions?\nL14: \nL15: Re-Interventions interrupt doom-scrolling in a target app after a set time, requiring another intervention to resume use. This is especially useful to limit time spent on target apps, and ensure that time spent is more intentional.\nL16: \nL17:  |\nL18: \nL19: # iOS Tutorial\nL20: \nL21: ## Step 1\nL22: \nL23: Open one sec → Customize → Re-Intervention.\nL24: \nL25: If you haven’t already, fulfill the request to grant access to the Screen Time API.\nL26: ## Step 2\nL27: \nL28: Find and select the app you’d like to set up a Re-Intervention for. In my case, I chose Facebook as an example.\nL29: ## Step 3\nL30: \nL31: Tap on Connect…\nL32: \nL33: This will bring up Apple’s Screen Time App picker.\nL34: \nL35: > ⚠️Only select one app here.\nL36: \nL37: Find the app you’re looking for by using the little arrow to unfold a category. Or use search.\nL38: \nL39: > 💡 Please note: Apple’s app picker is super buggy and unreliable. Especially when using the search it can crash frequently. I recommend to use the little dictation icon to insert the app name, this seems to work much better.\nL40: \nL41: ## Step 4\nL42: \nL43: Select and confirm the app. Now the Re-Intervention is set up!.\nL44: ## Troubleshooting\nL45: \nL46: ### What if I selected the wrong app?\nL47: \nL48: You can change the assigned app by tapping on Change app…\nL49: \nL50: ### What if the app picker crashes or does not show any apps?\nL51: \nL52: Please try again. Apple’s app picker is very unreliable unfortunately, sometimes it takes a few tries to get it working.\nL53: # Android Tutorial\nL54: \nL55: To set up the Re-Intervention on Android, open one sec → Settings → Re-Intervention. For each target app you can select if the Re-Interventions should be active or not. You can also set the maximum time interval that should be available when opening a target app.\nL56: \nL57: # Desktop Tutorial\nL58: \nL59: To set up Re-Interventions on the Desktop Browser extension, open one sec’s dashboard and select \"Customize\". At the bottom, select all websites you’d like to enable the Re-Intervention for:\nL60: ## Was this article helpful?\nL61: \nL62: Yes\nL63: \nL64: No\nL65: \nL66: Sorry about that! Care to tell us more?\nL67: \nL68: What was unhelpful?\nL69: \nL70: Submit\nL71: \nL72: ## Thanks for the feedback!\nL73: \nL74: There was an issue submitting your feedback\nL75: \nL76: Please check your connection and try again.\nL77: \nL78: [Button: Cookie preferences]\nL79: \nL80: cite13†Affiliate Marketing†one-sec.app cite14†FAQ†one-sec.app cite15†Website†one-sec.app L81: \nL82: cite16†App Store†apps.apple.com cite17†Play Store†play.google.com cite18†Browser Extension --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nIntentional App Switching [iOS / Android / Desktop] (https://tutorials.one-sec.app/en/articles/3310146)\nciteturn4view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn3view3\",\"id\":6}); Total lines: 113\nL0: cite0†Help & Tutorials L1: \nL2: cite1†Contact us†riedel.wtf L3: \nL4: How can we help?\nL5: \nL6: In this article\nL7: \nL8: cite2†iOS Tutorial cite3†Step 1 cite4†Step 2 cite5†Step 3 cite6†Step 4 cite7†Step 5 cite8†Step 6 cite9†Step 7 cite10†Android Tutorial cite11†Desktop Browser Extension Tutorial L9: # Intentional App Switching [iOS / Android / Desktop]\nL10: \nL11: Edited Sunday, October 26 2025\nL12: \nL13: Sometimes it’s necessary to leave social media and quickly switch between apps: to check contact info, a note, or a location in Maps.\nL14: \nL15: The goal of one sec is not to disrupt any productive workflows, that’s why we decided to offer a secondary Shortcut that can be executed when closing an app. This allows us to measure time between closing and re-opening the app, allowing you to re-open the app within certain time limits.\nL16: # iOS Tutorial\nL17: \nL18: cite12†Image†i3.ytimg.com L19: \nL20: This video is hosted on YouTube and requires cookies to view.\nL21: \nL22: cite13†YouTube Privacy Policy†policies.google.com L23: \nL24: cite14†View on YouTube†www.youtube.com L25: \nL26: Accept\nL27: \nL28: ## Step 1\nL29: \nL30: On your iPhone, open the cite15†Shortcuts app†apps.apple.com and go to the Automation tab.\nL31: \nL32: * * *\nL33: \nL34: ## Step 2\nL35: \nL36: Go to the Automation tab and select + to create another Personal Automation.\nL37: \nL38: * * *\nL39: \nL40: ## Step 3\nL41: \nL42: Scroll down and select App.\nL43: \nL44: * * *\nL45: ## Step 4\nL46: \nL47: Choose the app you’d like to configure the intentional app switching for.\nL48: \nL49: > ⚠️ Only select one app here. A separate automation is required for each app.\nL50: \nL51: Be sure that only “Is Closed“ is selected.\nL52: \nL53: At the bottom, select Run Immediately.\nL54: \nL55: Then, continue to the next page.\nL56: \nL57: * * *\nL58: \nL59: ## Step 5\nL60: \nL61: Select Create New Shortcut.\nL62: \nL63: > ⚠️ If you don’t see this option, you’re running an older iOS version. Please cite16†refer to the old tutorial .\nL64: \nL65: * * *\nL66: ## Step 6\nL67: \nL68: Search for “one sec” and select 🅱️ Log app closing (for quick app switching).\nL69: \nL70: * * *\nL71: \nL72: ## Step 7\nL73: \nL74: Tap App (must be selected⚠️) in order to re-select the previously selected app.\nL75: \nL76: The Automation won’t run without this.\nL77: \nL78: Then tap Done and you’re done!\nL79: \nL80: # Android Tutorial\nL81: \nL82: To set up intentional app switching on Android, open one sec → Settings → Intentional App Switching and select the time interval for which it should be active (e.g. 1 minute).\nL83: # Desktop Browser Extension Tutorial\nL84: \nL85: To set up intentional website switching on the desktop browser extension, click on the one sec icon in your toolbar / extension bar → Open Dashboard → Customize → Intentional Website Switching. Select the time interval that it should be active for (e.g. \"Allow leaving website for 1 min\".\nL86: \nL87: * * *\nL88: \nL89: Need help setting up one sec? cite17†Get in touch†riedel.wtf .\nL90: \nL91: ## Was this article helpful?\nL92: \nL93: Yes\nL94: \nL95: No\nL96: \nL97: Sorry about that! Care to tell us more?\nL98: \nL99: What was unhelpful?\nL100: \nL101: Submit\nL102: ## Thanks for the feedback!\nL103: \nL104: There was an issue submitting your feedback\nL105: \nL106: Please check your connection and try again.\nL107: \nL108: [Button: Cookie preferences]\nL109: \nL110: cite18†Affiliate Marketing†one-sec.app cite19†FAQ†one-sec.app cite20†Website†one-sec.app L111: \nL112: cite21†App Store†apps.apple.com cite22†Play Store†play.google.com cite23†Browser Extension --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBlock Apps [iOS/Android] (https://tutorials.one-sec.app/en/articles/3311298)\nciteturn4view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn3view3\",\"id\":9}); Total lines: 145\nL0: cite0†Help & Tutorials L1: \nL2: cite1†Contact us†riedel.wtf L3: \nL4: How can we help?\nL5: \nL6: In this article\nL7: \nL8: cite2†Blocking on iPhone cite3†Manual Block cite4†Quick-start a Block from a Widget or Control Center cite5†Block Overview cite6†Block Apps via Shortcut cite7†Block Apps on Android (Beta) cite8†Manual Blocks cite5†Block Overview L9: \nL10: # Block Apps [iOS/Android]\nL11: \nL12: Edited Monday, August 24 2026\nL13: \nL14: With one sec, you can't only intervene apps, you can also completely block apps (and websites!) when needed.\nL15: \nL16: * * *\nL17: # Blocking on iPhone\nL18: \nL19: There are different ways to block apps on iPhone. This tutorial focuses on\nL20: \nL21:   * Manual Block\nL22: \nL23:   * Block via Control Center/Lock Screen or a Widget\nL24: \nL25:   * Block apps via Shortcut\nL26: \nL27: For the other ways, please follow these links with regarding tutorials.\nL28: \nL29:   * cite9†Scheduled Block L30: \nL31:   * cite10†Block apps and websites via Focus Filter L32: \nL33:   * cite11†Block Apps and Websites after waking up L34: \nL35: * * *\nL36: ## Manual Block\nL37: \nL38: To start a Manual block, open one sec\nL39: \nL40:   1. and navigate to the Block tab.\nL41: \nL42:   2. Tap the + in the upper right corner.\nL43: \nL44:   3. Choose how long the block should be from the provided options (tap the + for a customizable time frame)\nL45: \nL46:   4. Choose if you want to Block Selected Apps/Websites/Categories or Block All (with selected exemptions)\nL47:   5. Select by toggling on or off if this should be a strict block or normal block: If strict mode is enabled you can't pause or leave the ongoing block before the time is over.\nL48: \nL49:   6. Press Start Block.\nL50: \nL51: Optional: You can also create a Recurring Block from the Block Tab by tapping Schedule. (cite9†Scheduled Block )\nL52: \nL53: * * *\nL54: ### Quick-start a Block from a Widget or Control Center\nL55: \nL56: If you want to start a manual block without opening one sec, you can also start a block directly from your Home Screen, Control Center or Lock Screen with:\nL57: \nL58: • our homescreen widget\nL59: \nL60: • one sec's control center toggle\nL61: \nL62: To add the widget to your long-press your Home Screen, tap Edit and \"Add Widget\" and search for the one sec widget and place it on your homescreen.\nL63: To enable the control center toggle, long-press your Lock Screen / Control Center to add the one sec block toggle.\nL64: \nL65: When you tap the widget or the control center toggle, the default selection of apps, websites, and categories on the Block Tab in one sec will be blocked.\nL66: \nL67: * * *\nL68: ### Block Overview\nL69: \nL70: Active blocks will be visible on your Lockscreen as Live Activity.\nL71: \nL72: In one sec they will be stacked over your Tab Bar. Also, If you navigate to the Block Tab you can see all your past, ongoing and coming blocks (manual, scheduled, focus filters) in a timeline for better overview.\nL73: \nL74: Also your Block Session Widget will show the ongoing time as well .\nL75: \nL76: * * *\nL77: ### Block Apps via Shortcut\nL78: \nL79: For more advanced use-cases, you can also block apps via the one sec \"⏳ Start Block Session\" Shortcut in the Shortcuts app – to create your own customized Block Session Shortcuts and Automations.\nL80: \nL81: Feel free to get in touch, if you are interested in more tech savy approaches. Our cite12†customer support†frederikriedel.typeform.com is always there for you to brainstorm with you and support you!\nL82: \nL83: * * *\nL84: # Block Apps on Android (Beta)\nL85: \nL86: On Android, you can choose between two different ways to block apps:\nL87: \nL88:   * Manual Blocks and\nL89: \nL90:   * cite9†Recurring Blocks (Opt-In)\nL91: \nL92: This tutorial is about how to start Manual Blocks.\nL93: \nL94: * * *\nL95: ## Manual Blocks\nL96: \nL97: To start a Manual block, open one sec\nL98: \nL99:   1. and navigate to the Block tab.\nL100: \nL101:   2. Tap the Start Instant Block / + in the down right corner and tap Instant Block.\nL102: \nL103:   3. Choose how long the block should be from the provided options (tap the + for a customizable time frame)\nL104: \nL105:   4. Choose which Apps you want to block and tap the checkmark to confirm.\nL106:   5. Select by toggling on/ off if this should be a strict block or normal block: If strict mode is enabled you can't pause or leave the ongoing block before the time is over.\nL107: \nL108:   6. Tap Start.\nL109: \nL110: Optional: If you are opted in, you can also create a Recurring Block from the Block Tab by tapping Schedule. (cite9†Scheduled Block )\nL111: \nL112: * * *\nL113: ### Block Overview\nL114: \nL115: In the Block Tab you can choose between Timeline & List to see your past, ongoing and coming blocks (manual & recurring) for better overview.\nL116: \nL117: Also: Active blocks will be stacked in one sec over your Tab Bar and are shown in your Notification Center and Lockscreen.\nL118: \nL119: * * *\nL120: \nL121: Need further help? cite12†Get in touch†frederikriedel.typeform.com L122: \nL123: ## Was this article helpful?\nL124: \nL125: Yes\nL126: \nL127: No\nL128: \nL129: Sorry about that! Care to tell us more?\nL130: \nL131: What was unhelpful?\nL132: \nL133: Submit\nL134: ## Thanks for the feedback!\nL135: \nL136: There was an issue submitting your feedback\nL137: \nL138: Please check your connection and try again.\nL139: \nL140: [Button: Cookie preferences]\nL141: \nL142: cite13†Affiliate Marketing†one-sec.app cite14†FAQ†one-sec.app cite15†Website†one-sec.app L143: \nL144: cite16†App Store†apps.apple.com cite17†Play Store†play.google.com cite18†Browser Extension --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBlock apps after waking up [iOS] (https://tutorials.one-sec.app/en/articles/3035330)\nciteturn4view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn3view3\",\"id\":11}); Total lines: 42\nL0: cite0†Help & Tutorials L1: \nL2: cite1†Contact us†riedel.wtf L3: \nL4: How can we help?\nL5: # Block apps after waking up [iOS]\nL6: \nL7: Edited Friday, June 19 2026\nL8: \nL9: Similar to the Scheduling of Interventions and Scheduled Blocking, you can also set up one sec to block apps after waking up.\nL10: \nL11: Open one sec’s settings and select Phone Free Morning. Select a time interval that one sec should block apps after waking up.\nL12: > You’ll need to grant permission to access your sleep data. one sec syncs with HealthKit to know when you wake up and will block apps after that for the selected amount of time.\nL13: >\nL14: > You can also enable Ignore Power Naps to avoid getting blocked out of apps after short naps.\nL15: \nL16: The Good Morning Countdown does not work? Follow this cite2†link for troubleshooting.\nL17: \nL18: Good Morning Countdown\nL19: ## Was this article helpful?\nL20: \nL21: Yes\nL22: \nL23: No\nL24: \nL25: Sorry about that! Care to tell us more?\nL26: \nL27: What was unhelpful?\nL28: \nL29: Submit\nL30: \nL31: ## Thanks for the feedback!\nL32: \nL33: There was an issue submitting your feedback\nL34: \nL35: Please check your connection and try again.\nL36: \nL37: [Button: Cookie preferences]\nL38: \nL39: cite3†Affiliate Marketing†one-sec.app cite4†FAQ†one-sec.app cite5†Website†one-sec.app L40: \nL41: cite6†App Store†apps.apple.com cite7†Play Store†play.google.com cite8†Browser Extension "
